<p class="puzzle-item"><b>FJF,S</b>
<br>
Any O in the letter grid is a typo, it should have been a P.  Whoops!
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>The Accumulator</b>
<br>
I scrapbooked the replacement sentences, I'm sure you'll know what to do with them!
<div style="width:850px;border:2px solid;padding:10px;margin-bottom:30px;margin-top:-10px;">My  ___  partner  ___  four Twinkies a day, then washes them down with a root beer ___.<br>
<br>
The gaming  ___  is the most visited room in my West End  ___, with potato crisps flying through the air and people's  ___  fingertips marking up the controllers.<br>
<br>
"Pick out a  ___  one", overheard Tom the sumo wrestling chicken, whose prospects were increasingly  ___, it was  ___  to see.</div>
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>The Cat's Meow</b>
<br>
The puzzle editors are very upset about this one.  Apparently, when they asked for an LED, they really meant LED, and not comb.
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>Memory Lane</b>
<br>
I have an impulse that "Reefs offer you kelp, but it varies" is important somehow, but it varies.
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>Takeout Ordering</b>
<br>In an attempt to reel in more American customers, some menu items have been changed:
<br>
<br>Chicken Velvet with Shrimp Soup &#8594; Breaded Chicken Fingers
<br>Dry Cooked Sliced Beef &#8594; Hamburger with Bacon
<br>Szechuan Pork Belly &#8594; St. Louis Style Pork Ribs
<br>Baby Shrimp with Szechuan Tomato Sauce &#8594; Shrimp Taquitos with Salsa
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>People and Places</b>
<br>
This puzzle is all wrong.  One of the clues was supposed to be "This University opened on the day of commemoration of King David the Builder", but I can't remember the rest!
</p>
<p class="puzzle-item"><b>Let's Get Submersible!</b>
<br>
